  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in New Jersey are $220M for FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 97.8% year over year. Award volume stands at 1,124 awards with an average award size of $195K. Year-to-year comparisons show prior fiscal years were much larger: FY22 was $9.5B, FY23 was $9.4B, FY24 was $10B, FY25 was $9.6B, and FY26 was $9.9B. The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Defense are the largest buyers so far in FY2027. The top vendors include CAPE-APTIM JV1, LLC and SK2 LLC. Remediation Services, Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services, and Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) are the leading industries by obligation. This snapshot covers partial fiscal-year totals only. Contracting activity appears concentrated: the top buying agencies and top vendors together account for a large share of the FY2027 to date total. State-level procurement teams and contractors should note that FY2027 totals are fiscal year to date, and that prior fiscal years had substantially higher annual obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $220M. Fiscal year totals were much larger in recent years: FY22 was $9.5B, FY23 was $9.4B, FY24 was $10B, FY25 was $9.6B, and FY26 was $9.9B. Obligations fell 97.8% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries dominate spending so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $85.1M and the Department of Defense obligated $41.3M. Remediation Services is the largest industry at $40M, followed by Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services at $32M and Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) at $28.3M. The top vendors include CAPE-APTIM JV1, LLC at $40M and SK2 LLC at $31.8M."
      }
    ]
  },
